<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
     <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
    <title>Add a new discovery</title>
</head>
<body>

<header class="site-header">


        <!--navigation starts -->
    <nav class="site-nav">
        <a class="brand" href="/">
            <img src="/journal-logo.png" alt="logo for the Website.">
        <span>The Other World Journal</span>
        </a>
        
        <ul class="nav-links">
            <li><a href="/login">Login</a></li>
            <li><a href="/signup">Signup</a></li>
            <li><a href="/discoveries">View Discoveries</a></li>
            <li><a href="/discoveries/new">Add Discoveries</a></li>
        
        </ul>
    </nav>
</header> 

<main class="container">
    <h1>Write your discovery</h1>



    <!--make the form to add the meal
        * different meal times: breakfast lunch dinner snack morning snack grazing emotional eating
        * date: 
        *where the user got/made the meal: home, ordered via app/delivery, went out to eat
        *rating: 1 - 5 stars 
        *place to list the ingredients 
        *place to put the poem 
        *submit button for the form 
        
        - where is all of this information going to go? To the /meals/new routes 
            * what kind of CRUD operation is this? POST
            
        - the names in the form can not be the same because they are used by Express to see which values are being submitted. 
        
         write your poem here. This is an example:

            "Upon my lips did I taste
            but the sweetest essence of life
            an apple red and firm 
            Gala perhaps --
            organic and true"
        -->

   

    <!--choice form-->
    <form action="/discoveries/new" method="POST">
       <label for="title">What did you discover?</label>
        <input type="text" name="title" id="title" placeholder="A doll that looks just like you...">

   <label for="location">Where did you find it?</label>
   <input type="text" name="location" id="location" placeholder="On the back porch..." required></input>

   <label for="discoveredOn">When did you find it?</label>
   <input type="date" name="discoveredOn" id="discoveredOn"   required></input>

    <label for="description" required>Describe what happened</label>
        <textarea id="description" name="description" rows="8" cols="100" placeholder="Describe the World you have found." required></textarea>
    </label>

    <label for="mood">What feeling did it create?</label>
       <select name="mood" id="mood" required>
            <option value="">Choose a mood</option>
            <option value="curious" >Curious</option>
            <option value="eerie" >Eerie</option>
            <option value="dangerous" >Dangerous</option>
            <option value="beautiful" >Beautiful</option>
            <option value="mysterious" >Mysterious</option>
       </select>


       <label for="braveryRating">How brave did you feel out of 5 stars</label>
       <select name="braveryRating" id="braveryRating">
            
           
            <option value="1">Not very brave</option>
            <option value="2">A little brave</option>
            <option value="3">Somewhat brave</option>
            <option value="4">Very brave</option>
            <option value="5">Extremely brave</option>
       </select>

       <label for="warning">What warning would you leave for another?</label>
   <textarea name="warning" id="warning" rows="5" placeholder="The hand seeks the Key." required></textarea>

       <button class="button" type="submit">Save Discovery</button>
    </form> 
</main>
</body>
</html>